    "buildCommand": "cd /Users/minsung.jung/myproject/offensive-security && git add frontend/src/components/FindingsPanel.tsx frontend/src/pages/InteractionDashboard.tsx && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(ui): type-aware FindingsPanel replaces stringly-typed log scan\n\nThe backend already bundles structured AgentResult.findings into the\nterminal status WebSocket event. The old dashboard ignored that payload\nand counted \"[finding]\" substrings in log lines instead, so the rich data\nemitted by parse_gobuster / parse_sqlmap / parse_nikto (and the legacy\nnmap open_port findings) never reached the user.\n\nNew FindingsPanel component groups findings by type with per-type rows:\n  - directory_found: path + status + size\n  - sql_injection:   GET/POST/COOKIE param + technique + payload\n  - web_vuln:        id (OSVDB-...) + message\n  - open_port:       port/proto + service + version\n  - unknown:         JSON fallback (never silently drops)\n\nSeverity is mapped to badge variants. InteractionDashboard adds a\nright-pane toggle between Findings and the legacy Event Stream so logs\nstay accessible. The findings counter in the top bar now reflects the\nactual structured count, not log-substring matches.\n\nFrontend tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"",
